Task: Easing curves (Phase 2, Track foundation-core_20260918)

Red phase: the test file was written first and failed because the module did
not exist. Green phase: eight tests pass.

What the tests pin down:
- Endpoints are exact for every curve, including the exponential ones whose
  formulas do not naturally land on zero.
- The decelerating form equals one minus the accelerating form of the mirrored
  time, checked across the range rather than at a couple of points.
- The plain curves never move backwards.
- The overshoot curve exceeds its target somewhere before settling.
- Time outside the unit range is clamped.
- Looking up an unknown curve by name fails loudly instead of returning
  nothing, which would surface much later as a confusing error.

Design notes:
- Curves live in a table addressed by name so presets can carry a curve name as
  data rather than a function reference.
- The overshoot constant is named rather than inlined; it is the knob that
  decides how far past the target the motion travels.
